        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER KNUTSFORD PARLIAMENTARY DIVISION. REGIS- TRATION of Pardarnetitary Electors, County Electors and Parochial Electors. 1898. NOTICE is HEREBY GIVEN, that CLEMENT ELPHINSTONE LLOYD, ESQUlRE,.having been appointed one of the Barristers to REVISE TEE LISTS y Elections within the a Circuit and hold Courts F NorthE L fEoCr WalesTr eOvßi Circuit,iaig n t hPeaLrwliiisaltims on aftka perarliameetary Electors, County Eli ctors and Parochial Electors, and also of the separate List of Persons entitled to ha elected Members of the County Council of tbe County of Cheereri though ma the n RD hNeuCrosui tno DIVIBION of the County Electors Roll of tee s COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places following, that is to say : On WEDNESDAY, the 21st day of September NEXT, e nti County.tentitled o tb foreon at 11 20 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the NATIONAL SCHOOL,DISLEY, for the several Parishes in the fol- lowing Polling Districts, viz :—Dsley Polling District Dieley, Lyme Handley, and Newtown. Whaley Bridge Polling District—Kettleshulme, 'renal!, and Yeardsley- cum-Whaley. On WEDNESDAY, the 21st day of September NEXT, at 2-45 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the NEWS ROOM, POYNTON, for the several Parishes in the following Polling District, viz. :—Poynton-witti-Werth Polling Die- trict —Poynton-with-Worth, and Woodford. On THURSDAY, the 22nd day of Septemb-r NEXT,at 11 45 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the SUNDAY SCHOOL, BOLLINGTON, for the several Parishrs in the following polling Districts, viz. :—Bollington Polling District— Bollington, Kerridge, and Pott Shrigley. Rainow Poll- ing District—Macelesfield Forest and Rainow. On THURSDAY, the 22nd day of S-ptemher NEXT,at 315 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the BLACK BOY INN, PRESTBURY, for the several Parishes in the forowing Polling Districts, viz. :—Adlington Polling District— Adlington, and Newton. 'Prestbury Polling District— Butley, Fallibroome. Mottram Et. Andrew, Prestbury, Tytherington, and Upton. On FRIDAY, the 23rd day of September NEXT. at 11-15 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the DRILL HALL, WILMSLOW, for the several Parishes in the following polling District, viz. i—Wilmslow rolling District— Bollintee. Styal, and Wilmslow. On SATURDAY, the 24th day of September NEXT, at 11-15 o'c'o-lt in the Forenoon, at the PUBLIC HALL, ALDERLEY EDGE, for the several Parishes in the fol- lowing Polling District, viz. r—Alderley Polling District, —Alderley Edge,Alderley Netherailderley Over, Chorley, and Watford Great. On MONDAY, the 26th day.of September NEXT, at 11-15 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the NATIONAL , SCHOOL, SIDDINGTON, for the sever,! Parishes in the following Polling District, viz. :—Siddington Polling District—Capesthorne, Chelford, Marton,. Siddingten, Snelson,Somerford, Boothe,Withington Lower, and With- ington On MONDAY, the 26th day of SEPTEMBER NEXT,at 2 15 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the CLUB ROOM of the BULL'S HEAD HOTEL, HOLMES CHAPEL, for the 3everal Parishes and Parts of Parishes in the following Polling District, viz. :—Holmes Chapel Polling Distr:ct— Brereton-cum-Smethwick, Byley, that part of the Parish formerly known as Byley-cum-Itatehouse ;. Church Hulme, Cotton, Cranage, Davenport,. Kermincham, Leese, Somerford, that part of the Parish formerly known as Somerford-cum•Radnor ; Sorosten, that part of the parish formerly known as Mooresbarrow-cum- Parme ; Sproston, that part of the Parish formerly known as Sproston,Swettenham and Twerniow. On TUESDAY,the 27th day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 10.30 o'cloek in the Forenoon,at the SEeSIONS HOUSE, 'KNUTSFORD, for the eeveral Parishes in the following 'Polling Diatric's, viz. :—Aston-by-Budworth Polling Dietrict—Ast on-by-Bud worth, Crowley and Pickmere. Knutsford rolling District—Beaton, Knutsford, Mere, 011erton, Tables' Inferior, Wily Superior, Tatton, and Toft. Mebberley Polling District—Marthall-cum-War- f ord, and Mobberley. Over Peover Polling District— Blackden, Gonstrey-cum-Bsznshaw,and Peover Superior. On WEDNESDAY, the 28th day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the CLUB ROOM of the BLACK GREYHOUND INN, LOSTOCK GRALAM, for the several Parishes and. part of a Parish in the following Polling Districts, viz. ;—Allostock Poll-. ing District—Allostock, Peover Inferior, and Peover Nether. Lostock Gralan; Polling District-Aach Dennis, Lostock Grolam, Plumley. Rudheath, and Whatcroft, that part of the Parish formerly known es Shiphrook. On THURSDAY the nth day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 11-30 o'clock in -the Forenoon, at the LARGE ROOM, GRAPPENHALL, for the several Parishes in the follow- ' ing Polling District, viz :—Grappenhall Polling District —Orappenhall, Latthford, and La•chfnd Without. On THURSDAY,. the 29. h day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 1 o'clock in the Afternoon at the CLUB ROOM of the London Bridge lon, Stockton Heath for the several Parishes in the following Polling District, v:z ton Polling District Appleton-with-Hull, Stockton Heath, and Stretton. On FRIDAY, the 30th day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 11-30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the MAGISTRATES COURT HOUSE, DARESBURY,for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz :—Doresbury Poll- ing District—Acton Grange, Daresbury, Rattan, Kekr- wick, Moore, Newton-by-Wrest:user, Preston-o'th-Hill, Walton Inferior, and Walton Superior. Whitley Polling District—Aratrobus, Seven Oaks, Whitley Inferior, and Whitley Superior. And for all and every the Parishes, Townships, and places (if any) within the raid Knuts- ford Division of the County of Cheater, for which Courts to Revise, the Parliamentary Electors' Lists, County Electors' Lists, and Parochial Electors' Lists therein, have not hereinbefoie been appointed.</p>
        <p>—.„ At the Courts for such —of the above-mentioned Parishes or parts of Parishes as are s.tua`a within the Parliamentary Borotn,4l of Warrington, the Barrister will under the above Notice, revise the Ownership Lists Only for such Parishes. All Overs,-ers and other Persons whose attendance may be neceseary,are lire by required to attend the said Courts 1 at the several times and placls aforesaid, at which the I Lists of their respective Parishes are hereby appointed to be revised, and all Overseen are required to produce in Court the Rate Books of their respective Parishes, containing the Poor 'Rates made and allowed during the period between the 5,h day of January. 1897, and the 15th day of July, 1898, and to bring with them copies of their Lists, and all Notices of Claims and Objections, and other Papers they have received, concerning the Registration of Parliamentary Electors for the Knuts- ford Division. and County and Parochial Electors of the said County of Chekter. REGINALD POTTS</p>
        <p>Clerk of the —Cheshire County Council. Chester, 24th august, 1898.</p>
