        <p>NORTHWICH PARLIAMENTARY DIVISION. REGIS- TRATION of Parliamentary Electors,County Electors, and Parochial Elia, tors, 1898. INJOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that DAVID ARCHER .1.11 VAUGHAN COLT WILLIAMS, ESQUIRE, hav- ing been appointed one of the barristers to REVISE THE LISTS OF ELECTORS in Parliamentary Elections, within the North Wales Circuit, will make a Circuit and hold Courts for Revising the Lists of Parliamentary Electors. County Electors and Parochial Electors, and also of the separate List of Persons entitled to be elected Members of the County Council of the County of Ches- ter, though not entitled to be on the County Electors Roll of the said County for the NORTH WICH DIVISION of the COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places following, that is to say : On MONDAY, the 19rh day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 11.20 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day, at the Town Hall, Winsford, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz : Wirisford (Over) Polling District—Over. Wins- ford (Wharton) Polling District—Wharton. On TUESDAY, the 20th day of SEPTEMBED NEXT, 'at 10-30 o'clock in the Forencon, at the TOWN. HILL, MIDDLE WICH for the several earishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling District, viz :—Middle- wich Polling District—Bostock, Bylev ; that part formerly known as Crorton and Ravenscroft : Clive, Simierton ; that part formerly known as Einderton- cum-Helme : Middlewich and Stanthorne. On THURSDAY, the 22n1 day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 11-45 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day; and on FRIDAY, the 23rd day of SEPTEMBER NEXT, at 10-45 o'clock in the fore- noon, at the MAGISTRATES' COURT HOUSE, RUN- CORN, for the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Poll:ng Districts, viz. : Aston-by-Sutton Polling District—Aston Grange, Aston-by-Sutton with Middleton Grange, Dutton, and Sutton. Halton Polling District—Halton, Nei tux, and Stockham. Runcorn North Polling District—That part of Runcorn called Run- corn North. Runcorn South Polling District—That part of RUCICOM called Runcorn South. Weston Polling Dis- trict—Clifton and Weston. On SATURDAY, the.24lh day of Septembrer NEXT, at 10 30 o'clock in the Forenoon ; on MONDAY, the 2601 day of September NEX T, at 10 30 o'clock in the Finemon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day ; and on TUESDAY, the 27th day of Sgitember NEXT, at 10 30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the MAGIS- TRATES' COURT HOUSE, NOII THWICEI, for the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz:--Barnton Polling District—Ander- ton, Barnton, Bartingten, Cogshall, Comberbacb, Little Leigh, and Marbury. Davenham Polling District— Davenham, Eaton, Leftwich, Moulton, Whateroft ; that 'part formerly known as the Parish of Whateroft. Mars- ton Polling Distriete-Budworth Great, Marston, and Wincham. Northwieh (Castle) Polling District—Hart- ,ford, and Nerthwich ; that part formerly the Urban part of Hartford, aid the Parish of CastleeNorthwich. Northwich (LeftwiW Polling District—Northwich-; that part-formerly the Urban part of Leftwich andiParish of Northwich. Northwich (Witton) Polling District- -Northwich ; that part formerly the Parish of Witton- eum-Twambrooks. Weaverbam Polling District—Acton and Weaverham-cum-Milton. Winnin4ton Polling Dia- trict—Northwich ; that part formerly tha Urban part of Winning'on ; Winnington ; that part formerly the Rural part of Winninston ; Winnington ; thatrpart formerly known as Wallerseote. And for all and every the Parishes Townships and places (if any) within the said Northwich Division of the County of Chester, for which Courts to Revise the Parliamentary Electors' Lists, County Elec- tors' Liste,and Parochial Electors Lists therein, have not hsreinhefore been appointed. All Overseers and other persons whpo.le:eastteefnodveaenaciedm, at be necessary, are hereby reqnuatiinrveded pteovisahtetsenevdethheerseabiyd d