        <p>The eleventh annual. Meal in alai; competitions; for the Championship of Lancashire and Cheshire wOA opened over the expansive green adjacent to the Dog and Partridge Rotel, Old Trafferd. on Saturday afternoon. The contestants War- rington (Cemetery) and Harptarhey have been connected with the county assoelation for several seenons. Warrinetoe (Cemetery) has been held to be a formidable combination from the period of their affiliation, and in their first and second years of connection gained a dintingeished niece in the Senior Competition aeries, winning the chief prize, as far As our memory serves, in their seeand and third season. Afterward! they ran no to semi-finals in both that and the ehamplinselp competitions. Last season Werrinetoea met ! Radcliffe in the flnal,and sueceeded in *airline the county iseP by a fair majority ilarparhey hare been steady but sure progress since firnt appearing as a county ogenizetion. Mr. W Rethwell, vice-president, of Lonoight and Croft's ! Bank, consented, at the express wish of the county executives to referee awl umpire the mateh, and chose for his belp-ena' e I Mr. A Thompson. of Crofts B ink and Bleier Bronghfon.The game was opened at 3.30. Allison, Ande-ton, Ashton and Williams being the first to represent Warringtoe being oopesed by Towers. Counsel, TA nor and Schofield respec- tively. Bx-charapion Allison nlw ivs had the measure of J Counsel. and the Warrincton was eneblee to gain one of the most substantial wins during the afternoon. It Andarton with jack in hand took a dailded teed Is the early stages of his game with C Towers, but changing his mark the *leper ! hey player was enabled to draw level, and at One Vase win stetnally in front. Anderton, however, pulled himself to!. gather and from the 22nd end Towers had shot his bolt, and ! the Warrington skipper gained a well deservel victory by ! five points. J Ashton was not favoured with the best of luck , in his game with G Tayl.r. and after the Warringtonian hail' shown up well at one period, holding the commandine lead of seven. Taylor managed to secure the jack at the 23r4 end and run out a lucky winner by live shots. This defeat was counterbalanee by fT Williams, who showed cannistent good form in hie game with 13 S.ehotleli. winning by five pants. Thus when the firer quertetta had finished Warrington enjoyed a lead by eighteen points. The greatest interest was taken in the game between T Bolton end J Crowther, and the reenit of game was a surprise packet for the Warringtonlans, B Aten tailed to play up to his reputation, and the " hero of the Scott Boyd" match was enabled to win by no fewer th,n 16 Points. Bolton's crushing defeat apparently had its effect, for though R Rathwell aewannted for G Ashworth by four points, the failure of A 3 Jones in his game with 3 Reeves by eight points. and G Bail by three points in his game with J Holland turned the match slightly in favour of HarpurheY. Ball played a rare plucky game, and at one period was no fewer than a dozen In arrears. Holland was fortunate in defeating two capital woods. and taking the jack scored good win. When the last set of players appeared Harpurhey were leading ey five points. B Taylor after making a coed fight with A 8 Smith up to the 19th :end never scored again. and was defeated by nine points. T. /Bitten eeve early pre,nlse, and In his game with Ir. Counsel enjoyed a Marl at one period Of five. The players pfeled at 15. and from this point Connsel took the jack and ran out winner by six points. T. Bridge gave every promise of making sap for the failure of several of Ms comrades and went off with a good l-ad He ftiPed to sustain the capital form, and a eteanve mark was responsible for Tornilnsen mitkinz up mech of the leeway, and Bridge only scored a victory by two points S. Bail also did sy .11 in the opening st-ges of his , game with S. Jones. hot he, too, failed at the close, and lost ' by eight points. Warrington were thin defeated 26 points and