      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT LEAGUE (2ND DIVISION).</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON OLYMPIC'S RE3ERVE v. WARRING.</p>
        <p>TON ALBIONS.</p>
        <p>The alms match was played on Saturday, 3rd Sep- tembar, at Mill-lane. :Toe Alblons won the toss and had the advantage of playing with the wind. Son after the kick off, A. Ellison, ran along the touch, and put In I a beautiful centre fr itn which Carman beaded a grand I goal for the Olympic's, tha Albions eqnalising from a penalty. Directly afterwards the Albion s Obtained the lead by 'coring a second goal; and at half-time were leading by 2 goals to 1 goal. On changing ends Griffiths scored a grand 'pal for the Olympic's who pressed the Albions tor the remainder of the game but without being able to score again. The game end:l In a draw of 2 goals each. LATCHFORD v. LATCHFORD BRITTANIA. . .</p>
        <p>These rival clubs m t oa the LatChfoTagrouni in their opening game of the season, when a streng eleven of La'chford opposd a weak team of the Brittasies. Ttle result being Latchford 3. B.u.vania nil.</p>
