      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0116" n="art0116">
        <head>ST. HELEN'S TOWN COUNCIL.</head>
        <p>ST. HELEN'S TOWN COUNCIL.</p>
        <p>THE TOWN CLERK AND HIS SERVICES.</p>
        <p>The menthly meetinl of the St. Helens Town Council I was held on Wednesday afternoon, the Mayor (Alder- man R. Pilkington) presiding. The Mayor, moved a resolution of sympathy with Mrs. H)pkinson and her family, which wag Seconded by the Deputy Mayor (Court-oilier Martin), and adopted: The standing Enders of the council were suspended in order that. on the recommendation of the cninmittee,the Wary of th) town-c'e:k (Mr. W. J. Jeeves) sh tull be raised to the maximum (£1000) as from April last, in- stead of by three yearly instalme its of £5O The Mayor moved the adoption of the recommenda- tion, an i said it was felt that the ser ?ices of the Town Clerk in the pro:notion of the new Corporation Bill in Parliament meritel semi recognition. By anticipating the maximum salary Mr. Jeaves would rec&amp;va this year £lOO extra, and next year an additional £5O extra. C""ill" Willis rno":d• awrrlment against tho proposal. He remarked that wh,n Mr. POlreed salary was hat rtised he (Mr. Willis) was not a monaber of the couecii, and thi therefore an opportualty of knowing real public opinion on the subject. It was then urged that the increase eho old be final, and under no circum- stance; should the arrangement b 3 deviated frorn. Town Clerk had done his work well, bat other officials had contrit.atlel their share and had an &amp;oat right to recognition. Be moved that the original resolution should not be amended as now recommended by the committee.—Coueoillor Morgan seconded the meal, meet. On being put tO the dote, CoundilldrilWlil, felorgagi Fisher, Peet, Brown, and Collins voted in favour of the awn in ,ot, and twelve voted against it. Several members did not votes,: and Councilldf itiorOan asked that all monabers preseat should be asked to Vote. The Mayor : The ameacloactnt is lost, and I eac't make thsin vote.</p>
