      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-09-09_WidnesExaminer_art0117" n="art0117">
        <head>STOCKTON HEATH.</head>
        <p>STOCKTON HEATH.</p>
        <p>paowNrwd tl'LttT iN TN CANAL.-00 Sunday afternoon about o'clock while several sehoil cbildten were playing with the chain of a barge moored near Lendlo Brit:lg.. Seckton Heath, a boy named Harry smikey, live years of Live, fell in the canal and was drowned before assitta:nce could be obtained. The body was ncovrrad two boars later. Mr. J. E. Worsler, coroner,coniucted an interest at the London Bridge Inn, Stocicon Heath, on Monday afternoon.—Xtry Alice Sinkey. mother of the decentsed, identified the body. She said that on Sun iay after coon her son came home from Sundt,' ec.hool, but he went out in company with his brother shortly afterwardef.—.Elward Sankey said that he and his brother were fishing in the 'Bridgewater Canal near London Heiden en Suhday afterncon, after they had come from Sunday school. Thera were a nun:o- ber of boats moored in the canal trY thl.i side, aril his brother got on one of them and began playing with the chain, which slipped and pulled him into the water. WitnetS informed a man who was fishing from the Canal bank near to, and when he arrived at' tli e spot the deceased had gone down. Witness afaerwards to'd his father.--P.S. Gosline: deposed ta the ncoveri of the body.which he said was found at seven o'clock the same evening.—A verdict of " Accidnatally. drowned " was returned.</p>
